The network commands that inherit this deadline (crates/fleet-git/src/mutation/network.rs:9,20,34):
```rust
self.command(CommandKind::Network).args(["fetch", "--no-write-fetch-head"]) ...
self.command(CommandKind::Network).args(["pull", "--no-edit"]).may_conflict() ...
self.command(CommandKind::Network).arg("push") ...
```
`Runner::new` is private and `output_limit`/`git_program` are the only tunables, so no caller can lengthen the deadline.

crates/fleet-git/src/rebase.rs:111-127
```rust
async fn run_reword_transaction(&self, commands: [GitCommand; 3]) -> Result<MutationResult> {
    let _guard = self.mutation_lock.lock().await;
    let mut outputs = Vec::with_capacity(commands.len());
    for command in commands {
        match self.run_reword_command(command).await {
            Ok(output) => outputs.push(output),
            Err(error) => {
                let _ = self
                    .runner
                    .run(self.rebase_control_command("--abort"))
                    .await;
                return Err(error);
            }
        }
    }
```
No comment justifies the discard, and this is a subprocess invocation, not a channel send. Contrast `crates/fleet-git/src/watch.rs:67-69`, which does carry the required comment:
```rust
// A pending wake already covers every path in the shared buffer.
let _ = wake_tx.try_send(());
```

