`fields[4]` is `%(symref)` (crates/fleet-git/src/read/refs.rs:36: `"%(refname:short)%00%(objectname)%00%(subject)%00%(committerdate:unix)%00%(symref)%00"`) and is never read anywhere in the function.

Real git 2.55 output, verified in a scratch repo:
```
$ git for-each-ref --format='%(refname)|%(refname:short)|%(symref)' refs/remotes
refs/remotes/up/stream/HEAD|up/stream|refs/remotes/up/stream/main
refs/remotes/up/stream/main|up/stream/main|
```
and for an ordinary remote:
```
origin|refs/remotes/origin/main      # short name is `origin`, not `origin/HEAD`
```
